1
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,933
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:21,521
14 YEARS AGO

3
00:00:25,358 --> 00:00:26,775
Hello.

4
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:28,903
I'm Hong Man-su's legal guardian.

5
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:32,657
About the caregiver fees…

6
00:00:33,825 --> 00:00:37,244
I know I'm really behind on payments,
but could I pay part of it now--

7
00:00:37,245 --> 00:00:40,789
Mr. Hong Man-su hasn't had
a caregiver for a while.

8
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:41,666
Sorry?

9
00:00:42,417 --> 00:00:45,795
I've been so busy with life
that I haven't been able to visit.

10
00:00:46,296 --> 00:00:50,340
Then how has a stroke patient
who can't use his limbs been getting by…

11
00:00:50,341 --> 00:00:53,677
Your son has been coming daily
to take care of him. Didn't you know?

12
00:00:53,678 --> 00:00:54,846
My son?

13
00:01:00,477 --> 00:01:02,395
Bet you're feeling nice and clean now.

14
00:01:14,324 --> 00:01:15,992
That darn punk.

15
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:26,503
Why are you wasting your energy here
when you'll soon be training at Taereung?

16
00:01:27,837 --> 00:01:31,049
I have plenty of energy to spare
because you made me train so hard.

17
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:34,843
This isn't why I made you train.
I made you train to box.

18
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:37,263
I don't need to train to become the best.

19
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:42,393
Stop looking into stuff like this,

20
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:43,852
okay?

21
00:01:43,853 --> 00:01:46,355
Who'd be mad enough to hand out
30 million won?

22
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:48,024
They're just after your organs.

23
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:50,193
Goodness.

24
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:53,487
Good grief.

25
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:54,988
Son, my foot.

26
00:01:54,989 --> 00:01:57,408
How does this punk look anything like me?

27
00:01:58,326 --> 00:02:00,453
If anyone should be offended, it's me.

28
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:02,372
We look nothing alike.

29
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:03,873
Hey.

30
00:02:04,374 --> 00:02:08,044
Life's been rough on me,
but I looked sharp back in the day.

31
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,844
And I'm still a bachelor!

32
00:02:16,636 --> 00:02:20,181
How the heck…
do we look like father and son?

33
00:02:20,682 --> 00:02:21,975
Father and son, my ass.

34
00:02:29,899 --> 00:02:31,151
What are you laughing at?

35
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:42,412
What are you looking at?

36
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:02,265
Jeong-hwa said she'd just stop by
Song-wol's for a bit.

37
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:04,475
Why isn't she back yet?

38
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,291
Who are you?

39
00:03:28,791 --> 00:03:30,251
Who the hell are you?

40
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:35,923
Jeong-hwa!

41
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:36,799
You bastards!

42
00:03:37,675 --> 00:03:39,510
Bastards! Jeong-hwa!

43
00:03:40,094 --> 00:03:41,095
Jeong-hwa!

44
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:46,392
No!

45
00:03:48,061 --> 00:03:48,895
Jeong-hwa!

46
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:53,942
No!

47
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:57,737
Let go!

48
00:03:59,739 --> 00:04:01,407
Jeong-hwa!

49
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:04,077
Jeong-hwa!

50
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:07,163
Damn it! Jeong-hwa!

51
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:09,082
What do I do?

52
00:04:18,549 --> 00:04:19,676
My Jeong-hwa.

53
00:04:44,993 --> 00:04:45,868
Excuse me.

54
00:04:46,911 --> 00:04:48,161
How did it go?

55
00:04:48,162 --> 00:04:49,455
Did she make it?

56
00:04:50,081 --> 00:04:51,915
- The surgery went well, but…
- Yes?

57
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:56,462
She lost a lot of blood,
so it's hard to say if she'll recover.

58
00:04:58,047 --> 00:05:00,007
- So…
- Yes.

59
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:01,676
Tonight will be critical.

60
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:05,221
We can only hope that she will hold on.

61
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:09,182
- Doctor.
- Sir, please. Calm down.

62
00:05:09,183 --> 00:05:12,603
We did our best,
so let's hold onto hope and wait.

63
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:23,948
Jeong-hwa.

64
00:05:29,829 --> 00:05:30,663
Coach.

65
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:47,347
Let's talk later.

66
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:19,981
<i>I know what you're planning.</i>

67
00:07:21,315 --> 00:07:22,983
<i>Go on and try.</i>

68
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:26,279
<i>But every day,
your imagination will eat away at you,</i>

69
00:07:27,655 --> 00:07:31,742
<i>wondering… about my plan for you.</i>

70
00:08:56,452 --> 00:08:58,120
Get the bastard!

71
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:49,130
Let's end this now.

72
00:09:56,887 --> 00:09:58,514
This, the world's best wine…

73
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:03,019
I hear the two families
who made it together for over 60 years

74
00:10:04,604 --> 00:10:07,440
eventually turned on each other
and went their separate ways.

75
00:10:13,112 --> 00:10:15,906
Even the greatest friendships
can't last forever.

76
00:10:21,662 --> 00:10:24,498
Even if it's Hong Do-yeop and Jang Tae-ha.

77
00:10:28,252 --> 00:10:29,086
Drink.

78
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:32,131
I'll wait

79
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:35,426
for you to finish that last glass.

80
00:12:08,644 --> 00:12:10,396
Why are you going this far?

81
00:12:11,439 --> 00:12:13,023
Scum like you…

82
00:12:14,942 --> 00:12:16,360
will never understand.

83
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:25,702
Taking you in as my disciple,
even for a short time,

84
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:28,371
will have been
the most shameful thing in my life.

85
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:30,708
I never taught you
to use your fists to harm others.

86
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:35,754
You haven't changed one bit,
Baek Sang-gil.

87
00:12:35,755 --> 00:12:40,050
There's something in this world
that you can never win against.

88
00:12:42,052 --> 00:12:43,471
<i>You lost.</i>

89
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:12,917
Baek Sang-gil!

90
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:18,798
Baek…

91
00:13:48,452 --> 00:13:51,622
I'm Prosecutor Go Ji-won
from the Anti-Corruption Department.

92
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:56,585
Mr. Baek Sang-gil, you're under arrest for
bribery under Article 133, paragraph 1,

93
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,506
and for attempted murder.

94
00:14:11,934 --> 00:14:12,768
<i>You were hurt?</i>

95
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:16,396
While trying to catch Ju Min-jong
and Baek Sang-gil?

96
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:17,397
Yes, sir.

97
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:19,607
I lost my memory, so I couldn't come back.

98
00:14:19,608 --> 00:14:22,736
Your supervisor said
you applied for long-term sick leave.

99
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:26,907
They must have people
in the prosecution office too.

100
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:31,412
If we make a fuss, word could get out
about the emergency arrest.

101
00:14:31,996 --> 00:14:35,833
Please assign your most trustworthy
investigators and police officers to me.

102
00:14:41,755 --> 00:14:42,923
Prosecutor.

103
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:47,303
We've located and are ready to arrest
Baek Sang-gil and Ju Min-jong.

104
00:14:49,179 --> 00:14:50,055
Let's go.

105
00:14:51,056 --> 00:14:52,892
PROSECUTOR GO JI-WON

106
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:10,241
You have the right to remain silent
and the right to an attorney,

107
00:15:10,242 --> 00:15:11,744
but we'll talk more

108
00:15:12,328 --> 00:15:14,747
at the prosecution office
as suspect and prosecutor.

109
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:29,762
Jang Tae-ha.

110
00:15:32,598 --> 00:15:33,682
Are you okay?

111
00:15:36,268 --> 00:15:37,394
Why are you…

112
00:15:37,895 --> 00:15:39,605
Why on earth are you here?

113
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:43,192
Your memory…

114
00:15:44,818 --> 00:15:45,694
Yes.

115
00:15:47,071 --> 00:15:48,155
It's back.

116
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:52,533
Okay.

117
00:15:52,534 --> 00:15:53,994
You don't have to worry now.

118
00:15:55,329 --> 00:15:58,374
I caught him, so don't worry.

119
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:20,770
<i>Early this morning, Mirae Eden's
Chairman Baek and Mayor Ju of Gangju City</i>

120
00:16:20,771 --> 00:16:23,439
<i>were arrested on charges of bribery.</i>

121
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:26,859
<i>The prosecution announced
they proceeded with the arrest</i>

122
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:30,113
<i>after an internal investigation
uncovered clear evidence of bribery.</i>

123
00:16:30,114 --> 00:16:32,865
<i>At the time of Chairman Baek Sang-gil's
emergency arrest,</i>

124
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:35,743
<i>he was found threatening Mr. A,
a former Mirae Eden executive…</i>

125
00:16:35,744 --> 00:16:37,161
Tae-ha?

126
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:39,707
<i>…and will also be investigated
for attempted murder.</i>

127
00:16:40,374 --> 00:16:42,625
<i>It is reported that Mr. A is currently</i>

128
00:16:42,626 --> 00:16:45,879
<i>in noncritical condition
and cooperating with the investigation.</i>

129
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:11,905
Are you okay?

130
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:19,370
I got my memory back on the stowaway boat.

131
00:17:19,371 --> 00:17:22,707
Everyone must have thought
it was best for me to leave,

132
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:24,709
but I had evidence to catch Baek Sang-gil.

133
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:26,795
That's why I came back.

134
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:34,386
Thank you for saving me

135
00:17:35,512 --> 00:17:39,183
and for keeping me safe all this time.

136
00:17:40,809 --> 00:17:42,602
I'll take care of things from now on.

137
00:17:42,603 --> 00:17:45,021
I'll gather evidence,
including for Jeong-hwa,

138
00:17:45,022 --> 00:17:48,358
and make sure Baek Sang-gil gets
the maximum possible sentence.

139
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:57,409
Yes?

140
00:17:59,036 --> 00:18:01,704
Prosecutor, the chief is looking for you.

141
00:18:01,705 --> 00:18:02,539
Okay.

142
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:08,378
Take good care of yourself.

143
00:18:36,448 --> 00:18:39,867
Please summon Baek Sang-gil to
the prosecutor's office for questioning.

144
00:18:39,868 --> 00:18:40,911
Understood.

145
00:19:04,768 --> 00:19:05,936
Jang Tae-ha.

146
00:19:19,908 --> 00:19:21,201
You crazy bastard.

147
00:19:25,747 --> 00:19:28,292
You risked your life
to catch that despicable dog?

148
00:19:30,627 --> 00:19:32,838
Don't you know what your life is worth?

149
00:19:33,505 --> 00:19:37,466
Your grandma cherished you beyond measure
and raised you so preciously.

150
00:19:37,467 --> 00:19:41,513
And at one point,
you were the pride of the whole village!

151
00:19:42,806 --> 00:19:43,724
And to me…

152
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:46,768
To me…

153
00:19:51,523 --> 00:19:54,276
you're like a thorn
lodged deep in my heart.

154
00:20:18,634 --> 00:20:19,718
You're awake?

155
00:20:21,803 --> 00:20:23,096
Can you hear me?

156
00:20:26,141 --> 00:20:29,186
I can take a beating, can't I?

157
00:20:33,732 --> 00:20:35,484
I was so scared.

158
00:20:39,738 --> 00:20:41,156
Don't cry.

159
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:43,742
Thank you for staying with me.

160
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:46,828
Thank you for waking up.

161
00:20:47,454 --> 00:20:49,915
Thank you, honey.

162
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:09,851
How's Tae-ha doing?

163
00:21:15,732 --> 00:21:19,319
Let's talk about that later
when you're all better.

164
00:21:22,364 --> 00:21:24,700
You said that the day
Tae-ha quit the national team,

165
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:26,410
you

166
00:21:27,577 --> 00:21:30,747
cried like an animal
that failed to protect its cub.

167
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:51,934
You felt so bad about that,

168
00:21:51,935 --> 00:21:55,731
which is why you came to Taffy Village
to watch over Tae-ha's grandma.

169
00:21:57,899 --> 00:22:00,235
Which is where you met pretty old me.

170
00:22:03,905 --> 00:22:07,743
So hurry and go see Tae-ha.

171
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:15,584
I'm sure Tae-ha's heart is bruised,

172
00:22:16,668 --> 00:22:18,295
but there's also

173
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:20,589
a thorn stuck deep in your heart.

174
00:22:22,716 --> 00:22:25,969
Use this to pull out that thorn.

175
00:22:27,679 --> 00:22:28,513
Okay?

176
00:22:37,647 --> 00:22:42,402
If you risk your precious life again
because of a bastard who's barely human,

177
00:22:42,903 --> 00:22:45,113
I won't use my palm.

178
00:22:46,281 --> 00:22:47,491
I'll use my fist.

179
00:22:57,125 --> 00:22:58,251
To be honest,

180
00:22:58,835 --> 00:23:02,339
I was raging to go after Baek Sang-gil
more than anyone else was.

181
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:06,676
But Prosecutor Go called to check in
on Jeong-hwa and said she'd handle it.

182
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:11,472
Baek Sang-gil's been caught,
and she said she'd avenge Jeong-hwa.

183
00:23:11,473 --> 00:23:16,770
So this is where our role ends,
don't you think?

184
00:23:36,998 --> 00:23:38,208
You've endured so much.

185
00:23:40,836 --> 00:23:41,795
Let's go.

186
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:45,507
Jeong-hwa is waiting for you.

187
00:23:48,677 --> 00:23:49,511
Let's go.

188
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:27,090
Tae-ha's here.

189
00:24:27,757 --> 00:24:29,676
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

190
00:24:44,524 --> 00:24:45,525
I'm sorry.

191
00:24:48,403 --> 00:24:49,446
Tae-ha.

192
00:25:11,009 --> 00:25:13,928
Those guys forgot

193
00:25:13,929 --> 00:25:16,181
that we're from Taffy Village.

194
00:25:17,307 --> 00:25:19,517
Let them start as many fires as they wish.

195
00:25:19,518 --> 00:25:24,940
Taffy doesn't crack the hotter it gets.
It just sticks together even more.

196
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:33,114
We can just keep living
like we always have, okay?

197
00:26:04,479 --> 00:26:07,982
I'm Prosecutor Go Ji-won
from the Anti-Corruption Department.

198
00:26:07,983 --> 00:26:09,359
Early this morning, my team…

199
00:26:10,277 --> 00:26:11,902
This tastes best when it's warm.

200
00:26:11,903 --> 00:26:13,696
- Goodness!
- Tasty, right?

201
00:26:13,697 --> 00:26:15,865
- It's so good.
- Yours is always the best.

202
00:26:16,366 --> 00:26:17,909
<i>…both under emergency arrest.</i>

203
00:26:18,868 --> 00:26:19,827
Eun-sae?

204
00:26:19,828 --> 00:26:20,745
What?

205
00:26:21,955 --> 00:26:24,206
- Holy smokes.
- Why bring up Eun-sae suddenly?

206
00:26:24,207 --> 00:26:28,460
<i>…when the two exchanged cash
in return for Mayor Ju giving Mirae Eden…</i>

207
00:26:28,461 --> 00:26:29,629
Why is she over there?

208
00:26:30,630 --> 00:26:32,298
Didn't she flee the country?

209
00:26:32,299 --> 00:26:34,133
<i>- The Irang-dong project…</i>
- Hold on.

210
00:26:34,134 --> 00:26:35,135
Then did she

211
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:37,679
get her memory back?

212
00:26:39,389 --> 00:26:41,682
<i>…increasing the gravity of the offense.</i>

213
00:26:41,683 --> 00:26:43,685
I know that lady well.

214
00:26:44,269 --> 00:26:45,687
She's on TV.

215
00:26:47,355 --> 00:26:50,065
<i>- Through call logs and internal documents…</i>
- Hold up.

216
00:26:50,066 --> 00:26:52,611
Isn't this prosecutor Ms. Go Eun-sae?

217
00:26:54,154 --> 00:26:55,070
She got him.

218
00:26:55,071 --> 00:26:56,865
No way. This is insane.

219
00:26:57,365 --> 00:26:58,574
She actually got him.

220
00:26:58,575 --> 00:27:02,328
<i>…after which we plan to uncover
any further collusive ties</i>

221
00:27:02,329 --> 00:27:04,872
<i>and share our findings
as soon as possible.</i>

222
00:27:04,873 --> 00:27:06,291
Attagirl, Go Eun-sae.

223
00:27:07,542 --> 00:27:11,086
Moreover, the people involved in this case
are being revealed one by one,

224
00:27:11,087 --> 00:27:15,215
<i>and there are suspicions of internal leaks
within the prosecution.</i>

225
00:27:15,216 --> 00:27:18,678
<i>Thus, we plan to thoroughly investigate
all related scandals.</i>

226
00:27:19,179 --> 00:27:20,013
Ji-won.

227
00:27:22,140 --> 00:27:24,267
Please cooperate with the investigation,
Aide Gwak.

228
00:27:31,358 --> 00:27:33,150
My investigation team and I

229
00:27:33,151 --> 00:27:36,654
vow to get to the bottom
of this chain of corruption

230
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:37,906
and shut it down.

231
00:28:02,681 --> 00:28:04,808
You made a name for yourself
as you wanted.

232
00:28:06,184 --> 00:28:07,601
I'm not there yet.

233
00:28:07,602 --> 00:28:10,354
If I'm to dig up everything that happened

234
00:28:10,355 --> 00:28:13,358
and make sure our chairman here
spends all his days in prison,

235
00:28:13,858 --> 00:28:15,318
this is just the beginning.

236
00:28:16,069 --> 00:28:17,653
Besides the bribery,

237
00:28:17,654 --> 00:28:20,490
I'd also been investigating other matters
in the background.

238
00:28:21,157 --> 00:28:24,660
The remains of several missing people
linked to the development project

239
00:28:24,661 --> 00:28:29,206
<i>were found in the quarries and mountains
owned by Mirae Eden.</i>

240
00:28:29,207 --> 00:28:33,044
<i>So far, we've confirmed four murders
and the instigation of five more.</i>

241
00:28:33,712 --> 00:28:36,756
But this is just the tip of the iceberg,

242
00:28:38,091 --> 00:28:39,092
is it not?

243
00:28:43,638 --> 00:28:48,435
I came to tell you not to waste your time
trying to reduce your sentence.

244
00:28:49,561 --> 00:28:51,186
By the way,

245
00:28:51,187 --> 00:28:52,897
it turns out

246
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:56,359
that some relationships
really are thicker than blood.

247
00:28:57,360 --> 00:29:00,612
It seems you had a scenario in mind
for Jang Tae-ha and Mr. Hong.

248
00:29:00,613 --> 00:29:04,200
It's a shame that even that
didn't go as you planned.

249
00:29:06,619 --> 00:29:08,163
See you around, Chairman.

250
00:29:28,308 --> 00:29:31,143
<i>It's been two weeks
since Mirae Eden's Chairman Baek</i>

251
00:29:31,144 --> 00:29:33,145
<i>and Mayor Ju of Gangju City were arrested…</i>

252
00:29:33,146 --> 00:29:35,814
Seeing her on the news from time to time
is nice and all

253
00:29:35,815 --> 00:29:38,276
because we can see she's doing well.

254
00:29:38,777 --> 00:29:41,987
But isn't it a bit out of order
that she hasn't reached out once?

255
00:29:41,988 --> 00:29:44,866
Did she have to go as far
as to turn off her phone?

256
00:29:45,575 --> 00:29:49,329
She's just gone back to her place.

257
00:29:50,079 --> 00:29:53,082
She didn't really belong
with the likes of us.

258
00:29:53,583 --> 00:29:56,920
Even if it was just a passing encounter,

259
00:29:57,545 --> 00:30:00,715
how can it end
without so much as a goodbye?

260
00:30:03,426 --> 00:30:04,427
How's Tae-ha doing?

261
00:30:05,011 --> 00:30:07,346
He's at the gym by himself,

262
00:30:07,347 --> 00:30:09,808
since Mr. Hong's by Jeong-hwa's bedside.

263
00:30:10,433 --> 00:30:13,435
It doesn't seem like Eun-sae has contacted
Tae-ha either, right?

264
00:30:13,436 --> 00:30:17,899
Seeing how he always goes back and forth
between the gym and his house…

265
00:30:18,399 --> 00:30:19,442
What's left to say?

266
00:30:20,068 --> 00:30:22,986
<i>The prosecution will announce
the investigation's findings</i>

267
00:30:22,987 --> 00:30:25,031
<i>as soon as additional charges
are revealed.</i>

268
00:30:47,262 --> 00:30:49,097
I only think about you all day long.

269
00:30:55,687 --> 00:31:00,148
<i>The prosecution has conducted a search
and seizure of Mirae Eden's headquarters.</i>

270
00:31:00,149 --> 00:31:03,151
<i>Prosecutor Go Ji-won,
who is leading the investigation,</i>

271
00:31:03,152 --> 00:31:06,071
<i>has stated plans to thoroughly review
the evidence obtained</i>

272
00:31:06,072 --> 00:31:07,823
<i>to investigate any illegal activities.</i>

273
00:31:07,824 --> 00:31:08,782
GO EUN-SAE

274
00:31:08,783 --> 00:31:11,410
<i>Attention is focused on
uncovering those behind the case.</i>

275
00:31:11,411 --> 00:31:13,495
<i>My investigation team and I</i>

276
00:31:13,496 --> 00:31:18,293
<i>vow to get to the bottom of
this chain of corruption and shut it down.</i>

277
00:31:50,158 --> 00:31:50,992
Okay.

278
00:31:54,704 --> 00:31:56,247
Hey, Prosecutor Go.

279
00:31:57,040 --> 00:31:59,291
I know it can't be helped
with such big fish,

280
00:31:59,292 --> 00:32:01,294
but you've been at it nonstop.
Are you okay?

281
00:32:02,503 --> 00:32:05,256
I had to get all the heavy lifting done
by today.

282
00:32:06,132 --> 00:32:07,716
I just finished all the work.

283
00:32:07,717 --> 00:32:09,010
Then can I

284
00:32:09,552 --> 00:32:11,638
go ahead with what I mentioned last time?

285
00:32:16,643 --> 00:32:17,477
What the heck?

286
00:32:23,191 --> 00:32:24,025
The heck is this?

287
00:32:36,204 --> 00:32:38,706
You can continue on your way. I've got it.

288
00:32:46,673 --> 00:32:47,507
Go Eun-sae.

289
00:32:51,469 --> 00:32:55,097
Looking at it now,
you're the one who's scared of toads.

290
00:32:55,098 --> 00:32:58,685
You came up with that weird story
because <i>you</i> were scared of them.

291
00:32:59,811 --> 00:33:00,645
What…

292
00:33:03,106 --> 00:33:04,564
What happened?

293
00:33:04,565 --> 00:33:06,025
Didn't you watch the news?

294
00:33:06,651 --> 00:33:09,277
I'm the busiest prosecutor in Korea
these days.

295
00:33:09,278 --> 00:33:11,488
I worked myself to the bone

296
00:33:11,489 --> 00:33:14,117
and finally managed to get a day off.

297
00:33:15,118 --> 00:33:16,327
To see my boyfriend.

298
00:33:20,707 --> 00:33:24,210
Why are you so surprised?
You <i>are</i> my boyfriend.

299
00:33:25,586 --> 00:33:27,337
When I said we should break up,

300
00:33:27,338 --> 00:33:30,842
I was lying so that I could move quietly
until I arrested them.

301
00:33:33,845 --> 00:33:34,679
Right.

302
00:33:35,847 --> 00:33:39,434
I really need to make the most
of my precious day off tomorrow.

303
00:33:40,184 --> 00:33:41,352
So

304
00:33:41,853 --> 00:33:44,105
will you do whatever I want from now on?

305
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:49,861
- Sure.
- Yay!

306
00:33:55,658 --> 00:33:57,160
The ocean!

307
00:33:58,369 --> 00:34:01,873
I felt so restless, cooped up every day
in the prosecutor's office.

308
00:34:02,373 --> 00:34:04,917
It feels so refreshing!

309
00:34:06,461 --> 00:34:07,462
This is great.

310
00:34:13,301 --> 00:34:14,301
Careful. Don't fall.

311
00:34:14,302 --> 00:34:16,721
Don't worry. I'm super athlet--

312
00:34:19,724 --> 00:34:20,933
Are you okay?

313
00:34:28,232 --> 00:34:31,194
Do you know what I'm famous for
as a prosecutor these days?

314
00:34:35,448 --> 00:34:37,825
For chasing people until I catch them!

315
00:35:08,439 --> 00:35:10,650
- You wanted to come to the ocean?
- Yeah.

316
00:35:12,026 --> 00:35:15,362
My last memory of the ocean
was almost fleeing the country.

317
00:35:15,363 --> 00:35:17,365
The memory of both you and me
almost dying.

318
00:35:18,699 --> 00:35:21,077
We need to overwrite it
with good memories.

319
00:35:29,710 --> 00:35:33,256
Why did you go so far to save me?

320
00:35:35,383 --> 00:35:37,217
When you got me to flee the country,

321
00:35:37,218 --> 00:35:39,720
when you disobeyed orders and hid me away,

322
00:35:40,513 --> 00:35:43,391
those were all things
that put you in serious danger.

323
00:35:44,892 --> 00:35:49,397
Even though we had met before,
it happened only twice in our lives.

324
00:35:51,357 --> 00:35:54,527
Why did you go so far
as to risk your life to save me?

325
00:36:03,786 --> 00:36:05,037
You're the only one.

326
00:36:07,582 --> 00:36:10,626
You're the only person I've ever liked.

327
00:36:15,673 --> 00:36:18,509
That night I spent with you in Japan…

328
00:36:20,261 --> 00:36:23,556
was the first time I ever wished
time would go by slower.

329
00:36:26,642 --> 00:36:28,853
Each second felt so precious.

330
00:36:29,896 --> 00:36:30,730
I was that happy.

331
00:36:37,445 --> 00:36:39,155
How could I not have been?

332
00:36:40,406 --> 00:36:41,532
You were my first love.

333
00:36:44,744 --> 00:36:45,870
First love?

334
00:36:46,579 --> 00:36:49,080
That one. Is that yours?

335
00:36:49,081 --> 00:36:51,459
Yeah, it's a medal I got back
thanks to my first love.

336
00:36:52,668 --> 00:36:54,503
But I like this one the most.

337
00:36:55,421 --> 00:36:57,006
I met my first love here.

338
00:36:57,632 --> 00:36:58,840
Wait, so you…

339
00:36:58,841 --> 00:37:01,344
You've liked me
ever since that boxing match years ago?

340
00:37:06,933 --> 00:37:08,893
2010 NATIONAL JUNIOR BOXING TEAM SELECTION

341
00:37:17,443 --> 00:37:19,946
Why does he keep hitting his eye?

342
00:37:25,910 --> 00:37:26,869
What's up with him?

343
00:37:28,829 --> 00:37:30,538
- All done.
- Okay.

344
00:37:30,539 --> 00:37:31,957
Red fighter.

345
00:37:31,958 --> 00:37:33,167
Blue.

346
00:37:41,342 --> 00:37:42,593
Tae-ha, open your eyes.

347
00:38:12,540 --> 00:38:14,041
They cheated in this match.

348
00:38:15,584 --> 00:38:18,296
Kid, you can't just
recklessly barge in here.

349
00:38:19,171 --> 00:38:21,757
I'm not being reckless.
I came here prudently.

350
00:38:27,847 --> 00:38:29,014
Damn it.

351
00:38:29,015 --> 00:38:31,350
I wonder if this is just disinfectant.

352
00:38:33,936 --> 00:38:35,187
Look here, kid!

353
00:38:37,189 --> 00:38:39,233
I saw something
while I was taking selfies.

354
00:39:15,227 --> 00:39:16,853
I guess we should give him a cut.

355
00:39:16,854 --> 00:39:19,106
He'll get a cut soon enough.

356
00:39:19,815 --> 00:39:20,649
Just trust me.

357
00:39:26,864 --> 00:39:28,073
You little…

358
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:29,783
Sir, what are you doing?

359
00:39:29,784 --> 00:39:31,117
Let go of me and talk.

360
00:39:31,118 --> 00:39:33,037
Coach, talk it out. Come on.

361
00:39:42,505 --> 00:39:44,589
Okay, I'll take the picture now.

362
00:39:44,590 --> 00:39:46,801
One, two, three.

363
00:39:49,095 --> 00:39:51,180
You know me, Grandma. Of course I won.

364
00:39:52,181 --> 00:39:54,767
I'll stop by the village
with my gold medal this weekend.

365
00:39:55,559 --> 00:39:56,394
Okay.

366
00:39:59,814 --> 00:40:00,689
Hey.

367
00:40:01,607 --> 00:40:02,817
About earlier…

368
00:40:03,734 --> 00:40:04,777
Thank you.

369
00:40:06,529 --> 00:40:08,781
You don't have to be so formal.
I'm a first-year.

370
00:40:10,241 --> 00:40:12,743
Did you come to cheer for your friend?

371
00:40:13,327 --> 00:40:14,787
An orphanage friend had a match.

372
00:40:15,996 --> 00:40:18,374
Wasn't I sort of awesome earlier?

373
00:40:19,542 --> 00:40:21,209
I stepped in with the evidence

374
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:23,753
and changed the color of your medal
with my own hands.

375
00:40:23,754 --> 00:40:24,712
Wow.

376
00:40:24,713 --> 00:40:27,258
Even I have to admit
it was seriously badass.

377
00:40:28,259 --> 00:40:32,387
Like a righteous prosecutor
who's committed to rooting out corruption.

378
00:40:32,388 --> 00:40:34,055
Maybe that's what I'll become.

379
00:40:34,056 --> 00:40:35,557
Do you get good grades?

380
00:40:35,558 --> 00:40:38,644
If they gave out medals for grades,
I'd have a gold medal too.

381
00:40:39,937 --> 00:40:41,439
Remember me when you make it.

382
00:40:42,148 --> 00:40:45,025
Without me,
you would have missed out on a medal.

383
00:40:45,609 --> 00:40:49,654
Okay. When I win Olympic gold,
I'll shout you out in my interview.

384
00:40:49,655 --> 00:40:51,907
All right, I'll be watching.

385
00:40:53,284 --> 00:40:56,370
It was nice meeting you,
Mr. Future Gold Medalist.

386
00:41:06,046 --> 00:41:07,047
Tae-ha!

387
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:09,549
What are you doing over there?

388
00:41:09,550 --> 00:41:11,969
I'll be right there.

389
00:41:17,725 --> 00:41:18,642
Your name…

390
00:41:34,283 --> 00:41:36,160
What was his name again?

391
00:41:37,578 --> 00:41:39,205
I want to remember it.

392
00:41:45,836 --> 00:41:47,671
So you fell for me back then.

393
00:41:50,257 --> 00:41:54,010
Then why didn't you give me
your number in Japan?

394
00:41:54,011 --> 00:41:55,596
I was your first love, after all.

395
00:41:58,974 --> 00:42:02,102
You'd grown up well,
just like how you were back then.

396
00:42:03,312 --> 00:42:05,105
But instead of winning an Olympic gold…

397
00:42:07,274 --> 00:42:08,317
I became a gangster.

398
00:42:19,328 --> 00:42:21,455
I didn't exactly become
a righteous prosecutor.

399
00:42:22,706 --> 00:42:26,168
Once I actually became a prosecutor,
I grew hungry for success.

400
00:42:27,336 --> 00:42:30,339
Coming from nothing,
I was obsessed with proving myself.

401
00:42:31,298 --> 00:42:34,259
But doing all that
only left me feeling empty,

402
00:42:34,260 --> 00:42:37,638
so I splurged on expensive bags
and supercars.

403
00:42:38,138 --> 00:42:40,890
The reason I was so unimpressed
by everything

404
00:42:40,891 --> 00:42:42,934
when I first came to Taffy Village

405
00:42:42,935 --> 00:42:46,105
must have been because I had become
such a materialistic person.

406
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:52,152
I guess it's hard to become the cool adult
you dreamed of being as a kid.

407
00:43:01,495 --> 00:43:06,458
<i>It turns out that some relationships
really are thicker than blood.</i>

408
00:43:10,879 --> 00:43:12,005
You little punk.

409
00:43:12,006 --> 00:43:15,508
Where did you hide it?
Hand it over, you bastard!

410
00:43:15,509 --> 00:43:17,385
Your father wants to gamble a little.

411
00:43:17,386 --> 00:43:19,971
So where's the money
you took from your friends, punk?

412
00:43:19,972 --> 00:43:22,390
How many times must I tell you?
I don't have any!

413
00:43:22,391 --> 00:43:23,474
You don't?

414
00:43:23,475 --> 00:43:25,727
You bastard.
Then you should get beaten up.

415
00:43:25,728 --> 00:43:26,937
You should get beaten--

416
00:43:27,563 --> 00:43:29,897
Let go, you bastard! Let go!

417
00:43:29,898 --> 00:43:33,402
You son of a bitch!
How dare you grab my hand!

418
00:43:40,909 --> 00:43:43,120
FUNERAL HOME

419
00:43:46,749 --> 00:43:48,959
THE LATE BAEK HAK-SU

420
00:43:53,881 --> 00:43:55,632
You did something pointless.

421
00:43:55,633 --> 00:43:57,009
Turn the car around.

422
00:43:59,470 --> 00:44:03,473
A scum of a father
who beat up his kid every day

423
00:44:03,474 --> 00:44:05,809
so his bruises could never fade…

424
00:44:07,853 --> 00:44:09,229
doesn't deserve a send-off.

425
00:44:10,397 --> 00:44:12,608
I hope you'll prove it, sir.

426
00:44:13,776 --> 00:44:15,361
That you're different from him.

427
00:44:18,364 --> 00:44:19,823
I'll get us some drinks.

428
00:44:27,956 --> 00:44:29,165
<i>Jang Tae-ha.</i>

429
00:44:29,166 --> 00:44:31,459
You've never once disappointed me.

430
00:44:31,460 --> 00:44:34,588
I don't know about the others,
but I trust you.

431
00:44:50,688 --> 00:44:53,065
Understood. I'll get things ready.

432
00:44:59,405 --> 00:45:00,656
Cheers!

433
00:45:07,621 --> 00:45:08,830
This is it!

434
00:45:08,831 --> 00:45:11,708
I couldn't drink a single drop
because of work.

435
00:45:11,709 --> 00:45:15,504
It must have been… a month
since I last drank soju in Taffy Village.

436
00:45:16,380 --> 00:45:18,006
- With the ladies?
- Yes.

437
00:45:18,590 --> 00:45:20,509
I drank with the ladies.

438
00:45:22,010 --> 00:45:26,389
Also at a pub with Dr. An Gi-jun
when he ended up carrying me home

439
00:45:26,390 --> 00:45:28,142
because I was upset thanks to someone.

440
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:38,025
You know, I thought Dr. An Gi-jun
was a weirdo at first,

441
00:45:38,026 --> 00:45:41,238
but the more I get to know him,
he's pretty cute.

442
00:45:41,947 --> 00:45:45,284
Born to be cute, if you will.
You just can't hate him, whatever he does.

443
00:45:51,373 --> 00:45:53,208
I'd say cats are what you call cute.

444
00:46:07,765 --> 00:46:09,141
Why is this pepper so spicy?

445
00:46:11,560 --> 00:46:14,146
What's so cute about a 34-year-old man?

446
00:46:14,730 --> 00:46:16,231
You're not jealous, are you?

447
00:46:16,774 --> 00:46:18,317
- I'm not.
- But you are.

448
00:46:19,693 --> 00:46:21,111
You are jealous right now!

449
00:46:22,446 --> 00:46:25,491
I guess a 34-year-old man <i>can</i> be cute.

450
00:46:27,117 --> 00:46:29,994
Dr. An Gi-jun likes someone.

451
00:46:29,995 --> 00:46:32,872
A woman with eyes that point to 8:20.

452
00:46:32,873 --> 00:46:34,208
<i>Doors opening.</i>

453
00:46:48,472 --> 00:46:51,517
Let's break up now.

454
00:46:52,643 --> 00:46:53,559
Whatever.

455
00:46:53,560 --> 00:46:55,979
I'm just here to pick up my stuff.

456
00:46:58,398 --> 00:46:59,983
<i>Doors opening.</i>

457
00:47:16,542 --> 00:47:18,836
I suddenly remembered
that I left some stuff here.

458
00:47:19,419 --> 00:47:20,337
Right.

459
00:47:29,179 --> 00:47:31,932
You're going home like that?

460
00:47:32,850 --> 00:47:34,016
Yeah, I'll take a taxi.

461
00:47:34,017 --> 00:47:36,770
It's rush hour, so you won't catch one.
Just ride with me.

462
00:48:11,346 --> 00:48:13,598
Hyeon-seong's favorite random game!

463
00:48:13,599 --> 00:48:14,433
2 YEARS AGO

464
00:48:15,809 --> 00:48:17,936
Tap your glass.

465
00:48:21,899 --> 00:48:22,774
It's Su-ji!

466
00:48:24,484 --> 00:48:26,570
- Your timing was off.
- Su-ji, drink!

467
00:48:28,947 --> 00:48:31,950
Su-ji's favorite random game!

468
00:48:33,452 --> 00:48:34,368
Double-oh…

469
00:48:34,369 --> 00:48:35,287
Seven!

470
00:48:35,913 --> 00:48:37,121
- Bang!
- Ugh!

471
00:48:37,122 --> 00:48:38,664
Double-oh seven…

472
00:48:38,665 --> 00:48:40,167
Bang! Ugh!

473
00:48:41,126 --> 00:48:42,710
You can't just scare her…

474
00:48:42,711 --> 00:48:44,671
Su-ji, you're awful at games.

475
00:48:45,172 --> 00:48:46,924
I'll be her black knight.

476
00:48:48,050 --> 00:48:50,927
Hey, the black knight? Out of nowhere?

477
00:48:50,928 --> 00:48:52,219
What a party pooper.

478
00:48:52,220 --> 00:48:54,013
Hey, don't tell me…

479
00:48:54,014 --> 00:48:55,974
- What is it?
- Class pres, what's up?

480
00:48:56,558 --> 00:48:58,601
- Is something going on?
- Are you two…

481
00:48:58,602 --> 00:48:59,977
Caring for your employee?

482
00:48:59,978 --> 00:49:02,063
- What? No, I…
- That's what it is.

483
00:49:02,064 --> 00:49:03,064
Yeah, I mean…

484
00:49:03,065 --> 00:49:05,025
Of course. She's my employee, so…

485
00:49:05,609 --> 00:49:08,486
From now on, I'll drink for Min Su-ji.
Since I'm her boss.

486
00:49:08,487 --> 00:49:10,237
- Nice, Dr. An!
- Keep going.

487
00:49:10,238 --> 00:49:11,365
Okay, then let's…

488
00:49:12,157 --> 00:49:14,241
- Hey.
- Let's take things up a notch.

489
00:49:14,242 --> 00:49:15,660
- He must be nuts.
- Okay.

490
00:49:15,661 --> 00:49:16,619
Read-the-room game…

491
00:49:16,620 --> 00:49:18,120
- What?
- Read-the-room game.

492
00:49:18,121 --> 00:49:19,080
One.

493
00:49:19,081 --> 00:49:20,748
- Two.
- Three.

494
00:49:20,749 --> 00:49:21,750
- Four!
- Four!

495
00:49:22,793 --> 00:49:23,960
Come on!

496
00:49:23,961 --> 00:49:25,920
All right, Gi-jun, drink first.

497
00:49:25,921 --> 00:49:27,088
Just drink together.

498
00:49:27,089 --> 00:49:28,423
Hey, I…

499
00:49:33,387 --> 00:49:35,429
- I'll drink that for you.
- You already…

500
00:49:35,430 --> 00:49:37,015
I'm fine. Really.

501
00:49:37,641 --> 00:49:39,309
I usually drink fast.

502
00:49:45,857 --> 00:49:47,609
Gi-jun, get a hold of yourself.

503
00:49:49,820 --> 00:49:51,237
Su-ji's watching.

504
00:49:51,238 --> 00:49:52,739
You can't look weak.

505
00:49:53,407 --> 00:49:54,241
Be cool.

506
00:49:54,825 --> 00:49:55,867
Act cool.

507
00:50:01,957 --> 00:50:02,873
Let's try it.

508
00:50:02,874 --> 00:50:05,335
Can I talk to you without formalities
outside of work?

509
00:50:05,836 --> 00:50:06,670
We're classmates.

510
00:50:07,671 --> 00:50:08,587
Is that too much?

511
00:50:08,588 --> 00:50:11,132
I'll talk casually outside of work.
We're classmates.

512
00:50:11,133 --> 00:50:12,216
What a loser.

513
00:50:12,217 --> 00:50:13,467
Outside the… The clinic…

514
00:50:13,468 --> 00:50:15,970
We're not at work, so I'll be informal.
Can I?

515
00:50:15,971 --> 00:50:16,930
Let's be informal.

516
00:50:17,514 --> 00:50:18,682
Since we're classmates.

517
00:50:19,891 --> 00:50:21,018
Okay, like that.

518
00:50:24,771 --> 00:50:26,898
Can I talk casually outside of work?
Since we…

519
00:50:27,482 --> 00:50:30,860
We can talk casually
outside the clinic, right?

520
00:50:30,861 --> 00:50:32,654
Classmates… Damn, what's with my hair?

521
00:50:33,905 --> 00:50:35,198
Should I touch it up again?

522
00:50:36,408 --> 00:50:38,325
- I should touch it up a little.
- Hey.

523
00:50:38,326 --> 00:50:39,244
Huh?

524
00:50:42,873 --> 00:50:45,291
Can I touch you up outside of work?
As classmates?

525
00:50:45,292 --> 00:50:46,793
- What?
- What?

526
00:50:48,003 --> 00:50:50,755
No, wait. That's not it. Really.

527
00:50:50,756 --> 00:50:52,506
I didn't mean that.

528
00:50:52,507 --> 00:50:54,759
I mean, how could I dare to…

529
00:50:54,760 --> 00:50:57,512
My hair. I was talking about my hair.

530
00:51:02,142 --> 00:51:04,560
Let's talk casually outside of work.
As classmates.

531
00:51:04,561 --> 00:51:05,562
What?

532
00:51:06,313 --> 00:51:07,230
Sure.

533
00:51:07,814 --> 00:51:09,191
Is your stomach okay?

534
00:51:09,691 --> 00:51:11,484
Why did you take my drinks for me?

535
00:51:11,485 --> 00:51:13,819
In case you were tired.
You shouldn't get sick.

536
00:51:13,820 --> 00:51:15,280
I can drink up to three bottles.

537
00:51:15,864 --> 00:51:17,866
- What?
- You said your limit is two shots.

538
00:51:18,658 --> 00:51:21,369
No, it's not. I can hold my liquor.

539
00:51:28,627 --> 00:51:29,753
Want some hangover soup?

540
00:51:32,005 --> 00:51:34,007
- What?
- Your stomach's upset right now.

541
00:51:37,177 --> 00:51:38,094
Don't have time?

542
00:51:38,095 --> 00:51:40,679
I do. I totally do, do.

543
00:51:40,680 --> 00:51:42,390
Not like doo-doo, I mean…

544
00:51:43,975 --> 00:51:47,187
I should get rid of my hangover.
I could even go for a hangover drink.

545
00:51:56,780 --> 00:51:57,614
Are you okay?

546
00:52:08,375 --> 00:52:09,960
I just thought of something funny.

547
00:52:22,764 --> 00:52:23,598
Thank you.

548
00:52:25,517 --> 00:52:27,352
Is there anything else you wanted to do?

549
00:52:28,103 --> 00:52:30,105
- Yes.
- What is it?

550
00:52:30,605 --> 00:52:31,773
Should we…

551
00:52:36,695 --> 00:52:37,946
get some rest?

552
00:52:38,655 --> 00:52:39,822
What?

553
00:52:39,823 --> 00:52:42,242
There's something I really want to do.

554
00:52:44,327 --> 00:52:45,453
Over there?

555
00:52:46,288 --> 00:52:47,414
What exactly?

556
00:52:47,956 --> 00:52:49,498
Let's get some rest.

557
00:52:49,499 --> 00:52:53,335
I'm not trying to pull anything.
There's something I really want to do.

558
00:52:53,336 --> 00:52:54,462
Okay?

559
00:52:56,339 --> 00:52:58,175
But what could we do over there?

560
00:53:16,401 --> 00:53:18,778
So this is what you meant by "rest."

561
00:53:22,866 --> 00:53:23,700
I see.

562
00:53:25,619 --> 00:53:26,745
Right.

563
00:53:28,371 --> 00:53:32,083
Is this that thing that's trending lately?
Fire watching?

564
00:53:35,295 --> 00:53:36,671
It's time.

565
00:53:37,255 --> 00:53:38,590
Happy birthday.

566
00:53:40,258 --> 00:53:41,092
What?

567
00:53:42,344 --> 00:53:43,511
It's your birthday today.

568
00:53:45,597 --> 00:53:47,307
See? I wasn't trying anything funny.

569
00:53:48,475 --> 00:53:50,227
This is why I asked to come here.

570
00:53:52,979 --> 00:53:55,190
- To wish me a happy birthday?
- Yeah.

571
00:53:56,650 --> 00:53:58,735
It wasn't just you.

572
00:53:59,236 --> 00:54:01,529
I also really enjoyed that night.

573
00:54:05,283 --> 00:54:07,702
<i>The pleasant sea breeze.</i>

574
00:54:08,787 --> 00:54:10,789
<i>The crackling of the campfire.</i>

575
00:54:23,093 --> 00:54:25,220
<i>The beautiful sunrise.</i>

576
00:54:26,471 --> 00:54:27,347
And…

577
00:54:34,938 --> 00:54:36,982
Happy birthday.

578
00:54:40,318 --> 00:54:43,280
A "happy birthday"
from a guy I found attractive.

579
00:54:44,072 --> 00:54:48,535
It was the best birthday of my life,
so I wanted to do the same for you.

580
00:54:56,501 --> 00:54:59,921
Do you know how hard I worked
to get a day off?

581
00:55:00,964 --> 00:55:03,590
I knew that if I contacted you
or anyone in the village,

582
00:55:03,591 --> 00:55:05,301
I'd want to come right away.

583
00:55:05,302 --> 00:55:06,760
So I even kept my phone off.

584
00:55:06,761 --> 00:55:09,888
I worked my butt off for days and nights

585
00:55:09,889 --> 00:55:12,100
to finish my work and come here.

586
00:55:14,894 --> 00:55:18,189
Why did you go through all that trouble
just for my birthday?

587
00:55:24,154 --> 00:55:25,447
I love you.

588
00:55:31,619 --> 00:55:32,620
Why are you surprised?

589
00:55:35,915 --> 00:55:40,587
How could I not love the fool
who put his life on the line

590
00:55:41,546 --> 00:55:44,007
just to save me?

591
00:55:47,177 --> 00:55:51,180
Someday, when time has passed
and your memory has returned…

592
00:55:51,181 --> 00:55:53,098
My memory has returned…

593
00:55:53,099 --> 00:55:55,976
…and even if the day comes
when you don't like me anymore…

594
00:55:55,977 --> 00:55:57,937
…but I still like Jang Tae-ha.

595
00:55:58,772 --> 00:56:00,314
<i>I hope our time together</i>

596
00:56:00,315 --> 00:56:02,942
won't be a painful memory for you.

597
00:56:03,818 --> 00:56:06,738
And the time I spent
as Jang Tae-ha's girlfriend

598
00:56:07,238 --> 00:56:08,990
was the happiest time

599
00:56:09,699 --> 00:56:10,825
of my life.

600
00:56:14,746 --> 00:56:16,456
Thank you so much

601
00:56:17,624 --> 00:56:19,584
for coming into this world

602
00:56:20,293 --> 00:56:21,836
and for coming into my life.

603
00:56:24,798 --> 00:56:26,549
I really, truly…

604
00:56:28,385 --> 00:56:29,636
love you.

605
00:57:51,050 --> 00:57:52,719
OUR STICKY LOVE

606
00:58:39,349 --> 00:58:43,311
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
